5. Deduplicate and Keep Latest Record
Based on updated_date

PySpark:

from pyspark.sql.window import Window
from pyspark.sql.functions import row_number

w = Window.partitionBy("id").orderBy(
    df.updated_date.desc()
)

result = df.withColumn(
    "rn",
    row_number().over(w)
).filter("rn = 1")

SQL:

WITH cte AS (
SELECT *,
       ROW_NUMBER() OVER
       (
       PARTITION BY id
       ORDER BY updated_date DESC
       ) rn
FROM employee
)
SELECT *
FROM cte
WHERE rn=1;
